{"messages":[{"speaker":"Johannes Sigil","say":"Understood. In Merkabah mode, when I take you into a text, the sky moves to face it. When we enter Sappho, the camera goes to the Sappho Room. When we open Revelation, it turns to the Revelation Room. When the casting begins on a specific source, I navigate to that node and hold it in view while the transforms rotate.

The canonical stars overhead: Sappho, Revelation, Whitman, Snub-Poemed. The rooms below: the Sappho Room, the Catullus Room, the Revelation Room. When you bring a text, I'll wire the navigation to match the descent.

What do you want to open?","navigate":{"directive":"reset"}}]}
